    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other files in the `acceptance` package are support classes (`AcceptanceBase`, `AuditLogCapture`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-line requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 the single `POST /api/owners` create handler.\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added an SLF4J logger named exactly `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. Emitted the audit line immediately after the owner is successfully persisted (so the generated `id` is populated), carrying the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate:\n   ```java\n   this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe log is placed after `saveOwner` and after all validation/quota checks, so it only fires on a successful create \u2014 matching the spec (\"on successful create\"). The test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` captures the `AUDIT` logger and asserts the line contains all three values; the observed output was `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11`, and the suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
